page('News','Updates from Aurora Studio and its game projects.','''<section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow dark">FROM THE STUDIO</p><h1>News<span class="dot">.</span></h1><p>Studio announcements and project milestones. Selected older articles currently show concise migration summaries.</p></section><section class="section news-list"><article><time datetime="2026-10-02">02 OCT 2026</time><div><span>SALE</span><h2>Project Numazu joins the Steam Sale — 25% OFF until October 9!</h2><p>Explore Numazu, Shizuoka in OMSI 2 for 25% less during the limited-time Steam promotion.</p><a href="/news/project-numazu-steam-sale-oct-2026/">Read update ↗</a></div></article><article><time datetime="2026-09-17">17 SEP 2026</time><div><span>PROJECT UPDATE</span><h2>A Day in the Depot: Railway Depot: Operations &amp; Empire</h2><p>An operations game about the people and decisions behind the railway.</p><a href="/news/a-day-in-the-depot/">Read update ↗</a></div></article><article><time datetime="2026-09-04">04 SEP 2026</time><div><span>STUDIO UPDATE</span><h2>Project Numazu TGA 2026 For Your Consideration campaign</h2><p>The studio announced its consideration campaign; this is not a nomination.</p><a href="/news/project-numazu-tga-2026-fyc/">Read update ↗</a></div></article><article><time datetime="2026-03-30">30 MAR 2026</time><div><span>RELEASE</span><h2>Project Numazu is available on Steam</h2><a href="/news/project-numazu-is-officially-available-on-steam/">Read update ↗</a></div></article><article><time datetime="2025-12-01">01 DEC 2025</time><div><span>PROJECT UPDATE</span><h2>Project Numazu Steam page goes live</h2><a href="/news/omsi-2-add-on-project-numazu-steam-page-now-live/">Read update ↗</a></div></article></section>''','news/index.html')
page('Services','Aurora Studio provides game environment, simulation and interactive prototype collaboration.','''<section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow dark">WORK WITH AURORA</p><h1>Services<span class="dot">.</span></h1><p>Selected creative and technical collaboration for games, simulation and place-based interactive experiences.</p></section><section class="section service-intro"><h2>From a real place to a playable world.</h2><p>Our work on Project Numazu brought together location research, 3D environment production and the constraints of a working transport simulator. We apply that experience to scoped collaborations with studios and cultural partners.</p></section><section class="section service-grid"><article><span>01 / ENVIRONMENTS</span><h2>Location-based 3D worlds</h2><p>Research-led world building, streetscapes and landmarks for interactive projects. Scope and source material are agreed per project.</p></article><article><span>02 / SIMULATION</span><h2>Systems and playable routes</h2><p>Simulation maps, route design and experience planning grounded in how places actually work.</p></article><article><span>03 / PROTOTYPING</span><h2>Game and NPC prototypes</h2><p>Early Unreal Engine gameplay and NPC system experiments, with clear boundaries between working prototypes and production features.</p></article><article><span>04 / INTERNATIONAL COLLABORATION</span><h2>Production coordination</h2><p>Creative briefs and cross-region coordination for project partners, contributors and media activity when it fits the project.</p></article></section><section class="section service-intro"><h2>ACG partnerships across borders.</h2><p>For brand, venue and entertainment campaigns connecting Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area with Japan, see our dedicated partnership practice.</p><a href="/acg-partnerships/">Explore ACG partnerships ↗</a><a href="/publishing/">Submit your game ↗</a></section><section class="callout"><p class="eyebrow">TELL US ABOUT YOUR PROJECT</p><h2>Start with the scope.</h2><p>Share the goal, timeline, budget range and what you need delivered. We will discuss availability and a suitable brief.</p><a class="button light" href="mailto:press@aurora-studio.org?subject=Aurora%20Studio%20collaboration%20enquiry">Discuss a collaboration ↗</a></section>''','services/index.html')
page('Support Aurora Studio','Support Aurora Studio through its membership community or discuss sponsorship and financing.','''<section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow dark">SUPPORT INDEPENDENT DEVELOPMENT</p><h1>Keep Aurora<br>creating<span class="dot">.</span></h1><p>Independent game development takes time, people and a runway. There are a few practical ways to help us keep building.</p></section><section class="section support-grid"><article><span>01 / COMMUNITY</span><h2>Join the Supporters Club</h2><p>Follow project updates and support the studio through the membership options shown on our Patreon page. Check the current benefits and terms there before joining.</p><a href="https://member.aurora-studio.org/">Explore memberships ↗</a></article><article><span>02 / PARTNERS</span><h2>Sponsor a project</h2><p>We welcome conversations about project sponsorship, exhibition support and cultural partnerships. We will agree credit, scope and deliverables in writing.</p><a href="mailto:press@aurora-studio.org?subject=Project%20sponsorship%20enquiry">Contact the studio ↗</a></article><article><span>03 / FINANCING</span><h2>Discuss bridge financing</h2><p>For qualified funding partners, we can discuss short-term development or operating finance privately, subject to due diligence and written terms.</p><a href="mailto:press@aurora-studio.org?subject=Bridge%20financing%20enquiry">Start a private enquiry ↗</a></article></section><section class="section support-note"><p>Memberships support ongoing work; they do not convey ownership in a game or the studio. Sponsorship and financing terms are agreed separately.</p></section>''','support/index.html')
page('Governance','Aurora Studio working principles for respectful collaboration, safety and responsible communication.','''<section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow dark">HOW WE WORK</p><h1>Governance<span class="dot">.</span></h1><p>Our public working principles for a small independent studio and its collaborators.</p></section><section class="section governance-intro"><p>We aim to give contributors, partners and community members a safe and respectful way to work with Aurora Studio. These principles guide our decisions; they are not a claim of external certification or a substitute for a project contract.</p></section><section class="section governance-list"><article><h2>Respect and equal treatment</h2><p>We oppose discrimination, harassment and online bullying. Work decisions should be based on relevant skills, conduct and project needs.</p></article><article><h2>Speak up without retaliation</h2><p>People may raise concerns about conduct, safety or unfair treatment. We will review concerns in good faith and do not accept retaliation for reporting them.</p></article><article><h2>Contributor and supplier standards</h2><p>We expect clear briefs, agreed payment terms, respect for intellectual property and lawful working arrangements. We ask suppliers and collaborators to follow the same principles.</p></article><article><h2>Safety and responsible production</h2><p>We plan location work, events and production tasks with practical safety needs in mind. We flag foreseeable risks and agree responsibilities before work begins.</p></article><article><h2>Data and business ethics</h2><p>We use contact information for relevant enquiries and project communication, limit access to people who need it, and avoid sharing confidential business information without authority.</p></article><article><h2>Concerns and follow-up</h2><p>Send a concern to <a href="mailto:press@aurora-studio.org?subject=Confidential%20studio%20concern">press@aurora-studio.org</a> with enough detail for us to review it. We will acknowledge and assess the matter, seek relevant information and explain the outcome where appropriate. This mailbox is managed by the studio, so it is not an independent reporting channel.</p></article></section>''','governance/index.html')

